※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4923 LANG_OPERATOR_NOT_DEFINED

※ A symbol the language gives no meaning and nothing defined.  The glyph is a
※ legal operator -- Unicode calls it one -- so what is missing is the definition,
※ which is what the message says rather than "unexpected character".

type Point = x : u8 ; y : u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let p: Point = Point(.x ← 1u8, .y ← 2u8) ⊛ Point(.x ← 1u8, .y ← 2u8)
    0u6
